Wait, v2(n/3^v3(n)) = v2(n) since 3^v3(n) is odd. So:
B = {n : v2(n) = 0} = {n : n is odd}
W = {n : v2(n) ≥ 1} = {n : n is even}

So by strong induction, all elements of E are in W!

Therefore, with 1 ∈ B:
- B = {odd positive integers}
- W = {even positive integers}

And by symmetry, with 1 ∈ W:
- W = {odd positive integers}
- B = {even positive integers}
